Do not send a JSON body with 204 responses

Backport of upstream change 1010872, patch set 1, commit
b7c268371b7c2dff15a043e8d7e70343b2d403af (master, 2026-10-16,
Change-Id I27e64ed08ea9dd230b8ec4a9f62f2be53210dc5a, Closes-Bug
#2171078). The change is not merged, and neither barbican 22.0.0,
23.0.0 nor master (cd590f1b) contains it. The cherry-pick applies
without a conflict on top of the barbican patches numbered before
this one.

Five handlers answer 204 and are exposed with `template='json'`:

- DELETE /v1/secrets/{id}/metadata/{key}
  (`SecretMetadatumController.on_delete`,
  barbican/api/controllers/secretmeta.py),
- PUT and DELETE /v1/project-quotas/{project}
  (`ProjectQuotasController.on_put` and `on_delete`,
  barbican/api/controllers/quotas.py),
- POST and DELETE /v1/secret-stores/{id}/preferred
  (`PreferredSecretStoreController.on_post` and `on_delete`,
  barbican/api/controllers/secretstores.py).

Each returns nothing. pecan (1.7.0 in the 2026.1 image, 1.8.0 in the
2026.2 image) renders the `None` through the json template as `null`,
and for a 204 it clears the content type and keeps the body, so the
answer carries `Content-Length: 4`. A 204 must not carry content (RFC
9110, section 15.3.5). uWSGI sends the 4 bytes, Envoy resets the
upstream stream with
`upstream_reset_before_response_started{protocol_error}` and answers
the client 502, and Barbican has committed the write all the same. In
the C5C3/playground cluster (Barbican 2026.1 behind Envoy Gateway
v1.10.0) all 6 metadatum DELETEs from 2026-11-17 14:17 to 2026-11-18
07:55 UTC were answered 502, and
barbican_tempest_plugin's `SecretMetadataTest.test_secret_metadata`
was the only failing test of every Tempest run there
(C5C3/cobaltcore#1811). The Tempest jobs of CobaltCore OpenStack reach
Barbican without a proxy, and no upstream test asserted the body.

The change replaces `@index.when(method=..., template='json')` with
`@index.when(method=...)` and puts `@utils.allow_all_content_types`
below it, the form `SecretController.on_delete` has
(barbican/api/controllers/secrets.py).
`ProjectQuotasController.on_delete` already carried the decorator and
only loses the template. The
template alone cannot go: the content types a handler accepts come
from its template, and without one pecan answers 406 to
`Accept: application/json`, which Tempest and python-barbicanclient
send. Measured on 2026-11-18 on the 2026.1 image with only the
template removed from `SecretMetadatumController.on_delete`: 406 for
`Accept: application/json` and for `Accept: text/plain`, 204 for no
`Accept` header and for `*/*`.

With the patch each of the five requests answers 204 with an empty
body for no `Accept` header, `application/json`, `*/*`, `text/plain`
and `application/json, text/plain, */*`, on both images. On the four
handlers that lacked the decorator, a request that accepts only a
non-JSON type got 406; it now reaches the handler and gets its
answer. The error answers do not change, because `pecan.abort` builds
them from the `Accept` header: 400 for a quota PUT without a body, 404
for a quota DELETE of a project without quotas and for a
preferred-store DELETE when none is set, each with a JSON body. The
patch needs no operator configuration.

The release note of the upstream change
(releasenotes/notes/no-body-on-204-responses-5b2e0c7d9a1f3e64.yaml)
travels with the patch, so that the patch touches the same paths as
the upstream change. The image installs the barbican package only, so
the note changes nothing in it.

Tests: the upstream test hunks travel inside the patch unchanged.
test_can_delete_secret_metadatum
(barbican/tests/api/controllers/test_secretmeta.py),
test_should_put_project_quotas,
test_should_delete_specific_project_quotas and the helper
create_a_project_quotas (test_quotas.py),
test_set_a_preferred_secret_store_when_no_error and
test_unset_a_preferred_secret_store_when_no_error
(test_secretstores.py) send `Accept: application/json` where the
upstream change adds it and assert `b''` for the body; the helper
sends no `Accept` header. With only the test hunks applied, 8 of the
52 tests of the three modules fail with `b'' != b'null'` on 22.0.0
and on 23.0.0; through the helper,
test_should_get_specific_project_quotas, test_pagination_attributes
and test_should_get_project_quotas_list fail as well. With the patch
all 52 pass.

Proof: tests/container-images/verify_barbican.sh (Test 12) sends the
five requests with `Accept: application/json` to the WSGI application
of the built image and asserts 204 with an empty body; the published
images without this patch answer each of them with `null`. Test 12
then sends the quota PUT without a body, the quota DELETE and the
preferred-store DELETE with nothing left to delete, and asserts 400,
404 and 404, each with a JSON object as the body.

The twins under patches/barbican/2026.1/ and patches/barbican/2026.2/
carry the same diff and differ in their Applies-to line only.

Applies to barbican 23.0.0 (2026.2).

Upstream status: proposed as
https://review.opendev.org/c/openstack/barbican/+/1010872.

